---
layout: article
title: Alerts and notifications
description: Review Appwrite monitor alerts, notify organization members, and use escalations to reach the right people when an alert keeps firing.
---

An alert records one period during which a monitor's condition is met or an endpoint check is failing. Appwrite opens the alert as **Firing** and marks it **Resolved** when the monitor recovers. If the monitor fires again after it recovers, Appwrite opens a new alert.

# Review and acknowledge alerts {% #review-and-acknowledge-alerts %}

1. In your project, open **Observe** > **Monitors** and select the **Alerts** tab.
2. Filter by **All**, **Firing**, or **Resolved**, then select an alert to see when it started and the usage reading or check result that opened it. For a resolved alert, you also see when it recovered.
3. For a firing alert, click **Acknowledge** to show your team that someone is handling it. The alert keeps firing until the monitor recovers. Acknowledging also stops any pending escalation steps.

{% only_dark %}
![Alerts tab with one firing alert and two resolved alerts, grouped by date](/images/docs/monitors/dark/alert-history.avif)
{% /only_dark %}
{% only_light %}
![Alerts tab with one firing alert and two resolved alerts, grouped by date](/images/docs/monitors/alert-history.avif)
{% /only_light %}

You can also acknowledge an alert by right-clicking it in the list, or from the **Open alerts** card on the monitor's page. To revert, use **Undo acknowledgement**. The count on the **Alerts** tab only includes firing alerts that nobody has acknowledged.

# Choose who gets notified {% #choose-who-gets-notified %}

Choose recipients under **Notify** when you create a monitor. To change them later, open the monitor and go to **Settings** > **Notifications** > **Recipients**. You can pick the **Owners** and **Developers** roles of your organization, or an [escalation](#escalate-an-alert).

Confirmed members in the selected roles receive an email and a Console notification when the monitor fires and again when it resolves. Members with a registered device can also get a push notification. Remove every recipient to keep alerts in the Console and use their [project events](#use-project-events) without notifying anyone directly.

Each monitor has a **Severity** of **Info**, **Warning**, **Error**, or **Critical**. Critical push notifications can use higher urgency on supported devices.

**Cooldown** sets the minimum time between two firing notifications from the same monitor. Set it under **Name, cooldown** when you create a monitor, or in **Settings** > **Notifications** later. Alerts are still recorded while the cooldown holds back notifications.

# Escalate an alert {% #escalate-an-alert %}

1. In your organization, open **Settings** > **Escalations** and click **Create escalation**.
2. Add steps with the roles or members to notify, and how long to **Wait** before each step.
3. Open the monitor and go to **Settings** > **Notifications**. In **Recipients**, click **Add**, select the escalation under **Escalations**, and click **Update**. An escalation replaces the roles the monitor notified before.

You can also pick an escalation under **Notify** when you create a monitor.

Appwrite follows the steps while the alert is firing. The escalation stops when someone acknowledges the alert or the monitor recovers. If the alert keeps firing and you undo the acknowledgement, the escalation continues from its next step.

# Acknowledge with a server SDK {% #acknowledge-with-a-server-sdk %}

To acknowledge alerts from your own tools, such as a chat command or an on-call integration, create an [API key](/docs/advanced/platform/api-keys) with the `alerts.write` scope and call `update`. Pass `acknowledged: false` to undo an acknowledgement.

{% multicode %}
```server-nodejs
const sdk = require('node-appwrite');

const client = new sdk.Client()
    .setEndpoint('https://<REGION>.cloud.appwrite.io/v1')
    .setProject('<PROJECT_ID>')
    .setKey('<API_KEY>');

const alerts = new sdk.Alerts(client);

const alert = await alerts.update({
    alertId: '<ALERT_ID>',
    acknowledged: true
});
```

```server-python
from appwrite.client import Client
from appwrite.services.alerts import Alerts

client = Client()
client.set_endpoint('https://<REGION>.cloud.appwrite.io/v1')
client.set_project('<PROJECT_ID>')
client.set_key('<API_KEY>')

alerts = Alerts(client)

alert = alerts.update(
    alert_id = '<ALERT_ID>',
    acknowledged = True
)
```

```server-dart
import 'package:dart_appwrite/dart_appwrite.dart';

Client client = Client()
    .setEndpoint('https://<REGION>.cloud.appwrite.io/v1')
    .setProject('<PROJECT_ID>')
    .setKey('<API_KEY>');

Alerts alerts = Alerts(client);

final alert = await alerts.update(
