```server-java
import io.appwrite.Client;
import io.appwrite.coroutines.CoroutineCallback;
import io.appwrite.exceptions.AppwriteException;
import io.appwrite.services.Alerts;

Client client = new Client()
    .setEndpoint("https://<REGION>.cloud.appwrite.io/v1")
    .setProject("<PROJECT_ID>")
    .setKey("<API_KEY>");

Alerts alerts = new Alerts(client);

try {
    alerts.update(
        "<ALERT_ID>", // alertId
        true, // acknowledged
        new CoroutineCallback<>((result, error) -> {
            if (error != null) {
                error.printStackTrace();
                return;
            }

            System.out.println(result);
        })
    );
} catch (AppwriteException e) {
    e.printStackTrace();
}
```

```server-rust
use appwrite::Client;
use appwrite::services::Alerts;

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let client = Client::new();
    client.set_endpoint("https://<REGION>.cloud.appwrite.io/v1");
    client.set_project("<PROJECT_ID>");
    client.set_key("<API_KEY>");

    let alerts = Alerts::new(&client);

    let alert = alerts.update(
        "<ALERT_ID>",
        true
    ).await?;

    println!("{:?}", alert);

    Ok(())
}
```

```http
PATCH /v1/alerts/<ALERT_ID> HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
X-Appwrite-Project: <PROJECT_ID>
X-Appwrite-Key: <API_KEY>

{
  "acknowledged": true
}
```
{% /multicode %}

To read alerts, call `list` with [queries](/docs/products/databases/tablesdb/queries) or `get` with an alert ID. Both need the `alerts.read` scope.

# Use project events {% #use-project-events %}

For project monitors, use alert events to integrate with [webhooks](/docs/apis/webhooks), [Functions](/docs/products/functions), or [Realtime](/docs/apis/realtime). The event includes the alert as its payload.

| Event | When it fires |
| --- | --- |
| `monitors.[monitorId].alerts.[alertId].create` | The monitor starts firing and opens an alert. |
| `monitors.[monitorId].alerts.[alertId].update` | The alert resolves, is acknowledged, or has its acknowledgement undone. |

To tell the `update` cases apart, check the alert's `status` and `acknowledgedAt` in the payload. The cooldown only applies to team notifications. Project events fire on every change.
